# Shell scripts MUST check out with LF endings. A CRLF shebang line
# ("#!/bin/sh\r") is not a valid interpreter path and the script fails
# to run on macOS, Linux, and WSL. Windows clones default to
# core.autocrlf=true, so without this line install.sh is broken for
# anyone who clones on Windows and runs it under Git Bash or WSL.
*.sh text eol=lf

# PowerShell is fine either way; normalise for a clean diff.
*.ps1 text
*.md  text
